Registering Your Application
First, visit the Genius API Client management page and create an API client for your application. This will provide you with a client\_id and a client\_secret that you'll use to identify your application to Genius. The redirect\_uri is used for authenticating Genius users with your application. You can change it later. The API Client will belong to the user account signed in to Genius when it's created.

Making Requests
The available endpoints are listed below in the resources section, along with embedded examples showing how they work and what they return.

Genius uses OAuth2 for authentication. All API requests must be authenticated. There are plenty of libraries available to help with this part of your integration. There's also a detailed guide below if you're committed to implementing it yourself.

